**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.AppContextTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ImportDialogTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`

**How to implement.** The two library windows share one verb box and one folder picker, and the app's import context suggests the configured catalogue-export folder (001 §G 'Exports' and 'Every path is overridable'; S2.4 interpretation 10: the catalogue-export location is carried in `DataLocations` until its reader arrives; spec 0048 R2 and S3.2 interpretation 6: the lower declaration serves both windows). Both windows behave as before. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`. (a) The body of `verbButton` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:889`, public since step 107) moves into the new public `verbButtonOn (id : ConstructorUiId) (label : ControlCaption) (onPressed : PointerPressedEventArgs -> unit) : IView`, which hands the press to `onPressed`, and `verbButton id label onClick` becomes `verbButtonOn id label (fun _ -> onClick ())`. (b) The public `pickLibraryFolder (owner : Window) (title : ControlCaption) (startOpt : FolderName option) (onPicked : FolderName -> unit) : unit` is step 101's `pickCatalogueFolder` body, moved, with the title and the start folder as parameters. It opens `owner.StorageProvider.OpenFolderPickerAsync` with `FolderPickerOpenOptions(Title = title.value, AllowMultiple = false)`. For `Some folder`, `SuggestedStartLocation` is resolved through `StorageProviderExtensions.TryGetFolderFromPathAsync`, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile` (`:3376`) resolves its folder. A confirmed pick passes the first folder's `Path.LocalPath` as a `FolderName`, posted on the UI thread, and a host without a provider changes nothing. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S3.3. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/LibraryWindowView.fs`: its private `verbButton` (`LibraryWindowView.fs:1020`) and step 101's private `verbButtonOn` and `pickCatalogueFolder` are deleted. Every call uses `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` or `MaterialsWindowView.verbButtonOn`, and Register catalogue folder… calls `MaterialsWindowView.pickLibraryFolder owner (ControlCaption "Register catalogue folder") None`. The look, the ids and the messages are unchanged. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/AppContext.fs`: the compose that `create` and `recreateLibrary` share (steps 89, 100) builds `catalogueImports` as `CatalogueImportContext.create` with `exportFolderOpt` (step 116) set to `Some locations.cataloguesFolder` (`DataLocations.cataloguesFolder`, step 81) by record update, so every library window the app opens suggests it. Every other composition (`DefaultStores`, `initWith`, the tests) keeps `None`. (4) Tests. `AppContextTests` gains `the app's import context suggests the configured catalogues folder for exports`: over an app context composed through `TestAppScope` (step 83: `testLocations`, `freshAppContext`), `catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt` is `Some` of those locations' `cataloguesFolder`, and `CatalogueImportContext.create (CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()).proxy`'s `exportFolderOpt` is `None`. Every `LibraryWindowTests`, `MaterialsWindowTests` and `ImportDialogTests` fact passes unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the shared pieces land, `LibraryWindowView.fs` MUST declare no `verbButton`, `verbButtonOn` or `pickCatalogueFolder` of its own, and the app's `catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt` MUST be the configured catalogues folder; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the app's import context suggests the configured catalogues folder for exports`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.
